  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights, activations and KV cache for the agent loop sit in Vera's LPDDR5X (SOCAMM) memory.",
      "focus": ["cpu-memory"],
      "dot": "cpu-memory",
      "explode": 0.4,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "cpu-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Vera's memory controller and L3 stage the tensors the GPU needs next.",
      "focus": ["vera-memory-controller", "vera-l3-cache"],
      "dot": "vera-memory-controller",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. NVLink-C2C carries them coherently to Rubin GPU 0 at 1.8 TB/s — one address space, no explicit copy in code.",
      "focus": ["c2c-link-0"],
      "dot": "c2c-link-0",
      "stage": "c2c-link"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. On Rubin GPU 0, resident weights and activations already live in HBM4 (up to 22 TB/s per GPU).",
      "focus": ["rubin0-hbm-dram-left", "rubin0-hbm-dram-right"],
      "dot": "rubin0-hbm-dram-left",
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. If the tile lives in the other die's HBM4, it crosses NV-HBI — invisible to software, as on Blackwell.",
      "focus": ["rubin0-nvhbi"],
      "dot": "rubin0-nvhbi",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. Data lands in the shared L2 cache on die 0.",
      "focus": ["rubin0-l2-die0"],
      "dot": "rubin0-l2-die0",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. TMA copies A and B tiles from L2 into shared memory, asynchronously.",
      "focus": ["tma"],
      "dot": "tma",
      "drill": "rubin-sm-detail",
      "stage": "tma"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Tiles sit in shared memory, ready for the Tensor Cores.",
      "focus": ["smem"],
      "dot": "smem",
      "drill": "rubin-sm-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. The Tensor Cores run the matmul under the 3rd-gen Transformer Engine, e.g. in NVFP4.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "rubin-sm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Partial sums accumulate in Tensor Memory, not registers. Steps 7–10 repeat along K.",
      "focus": ["tmem"],
      "dot": "tmem",
      "drill": "rubin-sm-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "11. Epilogue: results move TMEM → registers; CUDA cores add bias, apply activation, quantize.",
      "focus": ["register-file", "warp-scheduler"],
      "dot": "register-file",
      "drill": "rubin-sm-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "12. Results go back to HBM4 via TMA. Over NVLink-C2C they're visible to Vera; over NVLink 6 (3.6 TB/s) they sync with other GPUs in the rack.",
      "focus": ["rubin0-nvlink-die0", "c2c-link-0"],
      "dot": "rubin0-nvlink-die0",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
